## Why This Is Asked
Tests handling of exact-unknown counts under Kleene semantics and practical propagation in a small constraint system.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene 3-valued logic with exact U handling
- Constraint propagation with implication, and, or
- Backtracking search with pruning when F is derived

## Code Example
```javascript
// Kleene tri-valued evaluator (values: F < U < T)
const order = {F:0, U:1, T:2};
function not(v){ return v==='T'?'F': v==='F'?'T':'U';}
function or(a,b){ return order[a] >= order[b] ? a : b; }
function and(a,b){ return order[a] <= order[b] ? a : b; }
function imp(a,b){ return or(not(a), b); }

// test assignment P1=T, P2=U, P3=F, P4=T
const c1 = or(imp('T','U'), and('F','T'));
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale the approach to N predicates and quantify the number of U variables?
- How would alternative three-valued logics affect the propagation strategy?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical logical deduction and simple SAT handling in a controlled, small-domain setting.

## Key Concepts
- Implication with negation
- Disjunction
- Satisfiability search
- Backtracking basics
- Early termination on first valid assignment

## Code Example
```javascript
function isSat(A,B) {
  // Clause1: (!A => B)  == (A || B)
  // Clause2: (B => A)   == (!B || A)
  // Clause3: (A || B)
  return (A || B) && (!B || A) && (A || B);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend to three variables with similar clauses?
- How does short-circuit evaluation affect performance in larger clause sets?

